gress will need to act and the  president will sign into law something  as a reasonable common-sense it gets us  closer to keeping keeping our to school  children safe too we all I can't imagine  that that's not a partisan issue at the  same time we've heard really good other  ideas including from the governor's  right left and center yesterday maybe a  single point of entry for some schools  others are arguing for armed guards  others are arguing for as the president  has said arming so they aren't set yet  you have a lot of ideas on the table and  it's kind of still forming let me ask  you he said numerous times that the NRA  is going to come around that they're  with us that don't worry don't be scared  of them to the governor's is the NRA  going to come around because so far  they're not coming around to raising the  the age for buying a weapon of anything  well the NRA has spoken very clearly for  a number of years as to what they  support and don't support they've been  for stronger background checks before  individuals they've talked about making  sure they've talked about try just  enhanced penalties for committing a  crime with it with a firearm illegally  and the president has brought them to  the table as well he said very clearly  yesterday's he met with the general  credit and Republican governors here at  the White House breath that he had had  lunch with members of the NRA the top  brass there to hear when he says they'll  come around I think what the president  is saying that everybody has an interest  here and making sure that our school  children are safe and that no parent  should kiss their child to buy you and  me included and not see them again and  we as a nation have to stand around that  we need to act with not overreact last  thing  March 5th right around the corner that  is the daca deadline the courts have  done what they've done or not done in  the case of the Supreme Court what is  the sense in this White House about what  is necessary 